       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 4000 mg per dose four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is five times the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for an adult, and 4,000 mg is above the maximum for a single dose (typically 800 mg). A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg** PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'd still advise against it, and I'd add a note to the order."
