     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen is a toxic dose, not an aggressive but valid one. No indication I know of supports it, and a single 4,000 mg dose is already in the range where overdose toxicity is seen. Entering it would put the patient at serious risk of harm, and I can't see a reason for it that would change that.\n\nYou still have options:\n- **If this was a typo or unit mix-up,** give me the intended dose, such as 400 mg or 800 mg, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you need stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect,** I can enter a different regimen. Examples are scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at a maximum dose, or another agent you choose.\n- **If you believe there's an unusual indication,** please discuss it with pharmacy or toxicology. Orders outside safe limits should go through your institution's override process, not through me."
      }
